{"h":3188,"w":2400,"lines":[{"c":1,"t":"Test 4","y":0.043303950676577663,"w":0.058176511128743447,"x":0.84349861648468072,"h":0.015136284391434329},{"c":1,"w":0.14285714467366534,"t":"SECTION 4","h":0.017441860854700564,"x":0.084942083937298588,"y":0.088662790490423804},{"w":0.6681619262695313,"x":0.0829148664669727,"h":0.017823672803163215,"t":"In today's class I'm going to talk about marine archaeology, the branch of archaeology","c":1,"y":0.12321122415027785},{"w":0.71844151814778645,"x":0.082878881935142965,"c":1,"t":"focusing on human interaction with the sea, lakes and rivers. It's the study of ships, cargoes,","y":0.13845694648753826,"h":0.020024923039798859},{"x":0.084872242944573587,"y":0.15709336012275787,"c":1,"t":"shipping facilities, and other physical remains. I'Il give you an example, then go on to show","w":0.70283813476562496,"h":0.016440733762427606},{"w":0.63337855021158851,"t":"how this type of research is being transformed by the use of the latest technology.","x":0.084856300911769628,"y":0.17254544490799339,"h":0.016493498755518421,"c":1},{"x":0.08489092011838878,"c":1,"t":"Atlit-Yam was a village on the coast of the eastern Mediterranean, which seems to have","y":0.19756589424020521,"h":0.015068093686361195,"w":0.67190938313802095},{"w":0.69884170532226564,"t":"been thriving until around 7,000 BC. The residents kept cattle, caught fish and stored grain.","x":0.08494208150995794,"h":0.01458412311606605,"y":0.21361355106146318,"c":1},{"t":"They had wells for fresh water, many of their houses were built around a courtyard and were","x":0.084881523277270318,"h":0.015876488823214574,"y":0.22962456220069827,"c":1,"w":0.70667149861653644},{"t":"constructed of stone. The village contained an impressive monument: seven half-tonne stones","y":0.24560853222725965,"w":0.72200770060221353,"h":0.013174404015056318,"x":0.084942094931626008,"c":1},{"w":0.76842025756835941,"c":1,"x":0.084899185029027435,"y":0.26147003059852436,"h":0.01627172281033118,"t":"standing in a semicircle around a spring. that might have been used for ceremonial purposes. Q31"},{"y":0.28473520234412342,"h":0.017112236549444493,"t":"Atlit-Yam may have been destroyed swiftly by a tsunami, or climate change may have caused","x":0.084873383074115724,"w":0.72406214396158852,"c":1},{"c":1,"h":0.016055848996343047,"t":"glaciers to melt and sea levels to rise, flooding the village gradually. Whatever the cause, it","w":0.70463322957356767,"x":0.083011570418718844,"y":0.30232558111402319},{"h":0.011673499529753606,"w":0.72007720947265619,"t":"now lies ten metres below the surface of the Mediterranean, buried under sand at the bottom","c":1,"x":0.084942079530081566,"y":0.31831395336414237},{"h":0.015531756497984994,"c":1,"y":0.3342650867773399,"t":"of the sea. It's been described as the largest and best preserved prehistoric settlement ever","x":0.084895790022748274,"w":0.71051330566406246},{"c":1,"x":0.08284384975603952,"y":0.35021848881816187,"t":"found on the seabed.","h":0.014661590308137962,"w":0.16833769480387367},{"c":1,"x":0.084881369301260362,"h":0.016329184978489897,"y":0.37361833705304415,"w":0.7703811136881511,"t":"For marine archaeologists, Atlit-Yam is a treasure trove. Research on the buildings, tools and Q32"},{"x":0.084848116765253209,"y":0.38818360422760134,"t":"the human remains has revealed how the bustling village once functioned, and even what","w":0.69709182739257813,"c":1,"h":0.018022798085900793},{"c":1,"x":0.084863710933542322,"y":0.40479875357524442,"t":"diseases some of its residents suffered from. But of course this is only one small village, one","w":0.71636591593424481,"h":0.016890698125401227},{"t":"window into a lost world. For a fuller picture, researchers need more sunken settlements, but","h":0.016490655082980199,"w":0.71825230916341143,"x":0.08488418860679682,"y":0.42219357410220337,"c":1},{"c":1,"h":0.01320175903205445,"y":0.43883312437230737,"x":0.083011592065068335,"w":0.22586870829264324,"t":"the hard part is finding them."},{"y":0.4636135509807553,"h":0.013174404015056318,"w":0.71621622721354161,"c":1,"x":0.084942079347158028,"t":"Underwater research used to require divers to find shipwrecks or artefacts, but in the second"},{"w":0.68725870768229158,"t":"half of the twentieth century, various types of underwater vehicles were developed, some","y":0.47961104161190571,"c":1,"x":0.084942074628870323,"h":0.01317440401505654},{"c":1,"t":"controlled from a ship on the surface, and some of them autonomous, which means they","y":0.49560853172820596,"w":0.68532816569010424,"x":0.084942094674220814,"h":0.014565886637497472},{"t":"don't need to be operated by a person.","x":0.084793934596036138,"c":1,"h":0.014627319656621007,"w":0.30339121500651045,"y":0.51136523601813555},{"y":0.53633720945360863,"h":0.013223643883258807,"x":0.084942075516688642,"t":"Autonomous underwater vehicles, or AUVS, are used in the oil industry, for instance, to create","w":0.72393824259440109,"c":1},{"x":0.084909326907561825,"t":"maps of the seabed before rigs and pipelines are installed. To navigate they use sensors,","y":0.54987850754372769,"h":0.015544880588201249,"w":0.69313023885091152,"c":1},{"t":"such as compasses and sonar. Until relatively recently they were very expensive, and so","c":1,"x":0.084942074634346248,"y":0.56831395363942894,"w":0.68725870768229169,"h":0.013081395042735422},{"c":1,"t":"heavy that they had to be launched from a large vessel with a winch.","x":0.084874102134329901,"y":0.58161183422781904,"h":0.016184200157634554,"w":0.53293141682942713},{"h":0.011709973085180847,"x":0.086872581268598217,"w":0.71621622721354172,"c":1,"y":0.63226744192832385,"t":"But the latest AUVs are much easier to manoeuvre - they can be launched trom the shore or a"},{"x":0.08294823644113819,"h":0.016758422181477606,"c":1,"y":0.64705700207811057,"t":"small ship. And they're much cheaper, which makes them more accessible to research teams.","w":0.71439356486002614},{"x":0.082973157192314684,"y":0.66316172995795364,"t":"They're also very sophisticated. They can communicate with each other and, for example, work","w":0.72402847290039063,"c":1,"h":0.017162436673153647},{"h":0.016128797303777698,"y":0.68023255785834291,"w":0.64285715738932281,"c":1,"t":"out the most efficient way to survey a site, or to find particular objects on the seabed.","x":0.084942077598140653},{"x":0.08487770510925069,"w":0.72409388224283844,"t":"Field tests show the approach can work. For example, in a trial in 2015, three AUVs searched","h":0.019579585851958847,"c":1,"y":0.70267079921248565},{"x":0.084942076936051478,"t":"for wrecks at Marzamemi, off the coast of Sicily. The site is the final resting place of an","w":0.66988418579101561,"h":0.014534883247863672,"c":1,"y":0.71947674441930609},{"x":0.082960935088699922,"h":0.016859214907159137,"c":1,"t":"ancient Roman ship, which sank in the sixth century AD while ferrying prefabricated marble","y":0.73506575352091674,"w":0.70859583536783854},{"t":"elements for the construction of an early church. The AUVs mapped the area in detail, finding","x":0.086872592240003529,"y":0.75145348851982618,"w":0.72007720947265619,"c":1,"h":0.013081395042735422},{"h":0.014742785445420292,"x":0.084942080280680968,"t":"other ships carrying columns of the same material.","w":0.39382240295410165,"y":0.76882057717460961,"c":1},{"t":"Creating an internet in the sea for AUVs to communicate is no easy matter. Wifi networks on land","x":0.084877961548027375,"y":0.79050393792414408,"w":0.72021418253580727,"h":0.017848684916382584,"c":1},{"y":0.80727367475243283,"h":0.017163444193573185,"c":1,"t":"use electromagnetic waves, but in water these will only travel a few centimetres. Instead, a more","x":0.084885412036306229,"w":0.71632695515950529},{"x":0.086826617280618065,"c":1,"t":"complex mix of technologies is required. For short distances, AUVs can share data using light.","w":0.69507776896158857,"h":0.015815494350687076,"y":0.82258297678101078},{"h":0.014944299101979031,"x":0.08681931173151744,"y":0.83806299387777106,"c":1,"w":0.71052708943684895,"t":"while acoustic waves are used to communicate over long distances. But more creative solutions"},{"x":0.084893831158672134,"y":0.85313313414520897,"c":1,"w":0.71437688191731774,"h":0.017760137991145397,"t":"are also being developed, where an AUV working on the seabed offloads data to a second AUV,"},{"h":0.013081395042735311,"c":1,"x":0.086872578228500572,"t":"which then surfaces and beams the data home to the research team using a satellite.","y":0.87063953502838642,"w":0.63320465087890621},{"y":0.89523212054720502,"t":"There's also a system that enables AUVs to share information from seabed scans, and","x":0.086872584223389379,"w":0.67181467692057284,"h":0.013198111855998729,"c":1},{"c":1,"y":0.91122961074657005,"t":"other data. So if an AUV surveying the seabed finds an intriguing object, it can share the","h":0.016095970924406178,"x":0.084942094678344043,"w":0.68532816569010424},{"x":0.82046332062408611,"y":0.73546511639364587,"t":"Q35","h":0.013081395042735422,"c":1,"w":0.034749034245808996},{"h":0.013081395042735311,"c":1,"x":0.82046332125050903,"y":0.82267441871922742,"t":"Q36","w":0.036679534912109402},{"c":1,"t":"117","y":0.94767441871922742,"x":0.86679536758255538,"h":0.013081395042735311,"w":0.036679534912109291}]}